old=next(l for l in before.split('\n')if l.startswith('**The EU small business scheme.**'))
rep(old,'**The EU small business scheme.** A German business seeking the small business exemption in another member state must apply electronically for the special reporting procedure at the Bundeszentralamt für Steuern (BZSt), which issues a small-business identification number (§ 19a(1) UStG). Its EU-wide annual turnover must not exceed EUR 100,000 in either the previous or current year; it must also meet the actual exemption conditions of each host state and the no-duplicate-procedure-registration condition in § 19a(1) no. 4. A BZSt number and the EU turnover test alone do not establish host-state exemption. It files a quarterly turnover report with the BZSt within one month after each quarter (§ 19a(3)). It must tell the BZSt within 15 working days if EU turnover passes EUR 100,000; participation ends at that point (§ 19a(4)). A business based elsewhere in the EU can use Germany\'s exemption only if the incorporated German § 19(1) limits also hold: German total turnover under § 19(2) at most EUR 25,000 in the preceding year and at most EUR 100,000 in the current year. It additionally needs EU-wide annual turnover at most EUR 100,000 in both years and the home-state small-business number valid for that German exemption (§ 19(4)).','R23')
old=next(l for l in before.split('\n')if l.startswith('**Small business: what counts.**'))
rep(old,'**Small business: what counts.** Total turnover is the sum of taxable supplies counted on receipts, less the two distinct exempt-supply categories in § 19(2): no. 1 subtracts supplies exempt under § 4 no. 8(i), no. 9(b) and nos. 11–29; no. 2 subtracts supplies exempt under § 4 no. 8(a)–(h), no. 9(a) and no. 10 only if they are ancillary supplies (Hilfsumsätze). Main financial or insurance activity in that second category is not automatically subtracted; establish ancillary status from the actual activity, without an invented numerical test. Sales of fixed assets are excluded separately. Supplies on which the customer owes the tax under § 13b count in; services the small business buys under § 13b do not (UStAE 19.2(2)). A small business still owes VAT on imports, intra-Community acquisitions and reverse-charge purchases (UStAE 19.1(1)).','R24')
old=next(l for l in before.split('\n')if l.startswith('**Input tax correction (§ 15a UStG).**'))
